PhaseShift: real int8 dot4 instruction in SimX (decode + execute), custom-3 opcode 0x7B (Opcode::EXT4, defined but unused upstream).
Applied ONLY to the fourth tree vortex-trees/psdot (scripts/mk_vortex_tree.sh --patchset ps --name psdot, then git apply --index). Never part of the base/ps patchsets.
  DOT4    (funct7=0): rd  = sum_k int8(rs1.byte[k]) * int8(rs2.byte[k])          2 integer register reads
  DOT4ACC (funct7=1): rd += sum_k int8(rs1.byte[k]) * int8(rs2.byte[k])          3 integer register reads (rd is the third source)
Executed on the existing ALU block as MdvType::DOT4/DOT4ACC: latency kDot4Latency = PS_DOT4_LATENCY (default 3 = kMulDivLatency, the MUL pipe;
build with -DPS_DOT4_LATENCY=4 via CONFIGS for one more adder-tree stage). Third source read: SimX fetches
the operand VALUES in one step (operands.cpp), but its TIMING model charges every source read through the 4-bank GPR conflict model (OpcUnit::on_tick ->
compute_bank_conflicts(), opc_unit.cpp:52-88: one stall per pair of non-x0 sources in the same bank, the pair loop covers all three sources), as for FMA, AMOCAS
and WGATHER; Vortex RTL already routes rs3_data to the integer ALU (hw/rtl/core/VX_alu_int.sv:167). Unmodeled: datapath area / timing / power of the four
8x8 multipliers plus the adder tree, and latency >= 5. DOT4 + add (2 reads) remains the conservative floor. RTL is NOT changed
(see patches/vortex/rtl/ for the synthesis-only RTL datapath).

